--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SUMMARY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI FeedbackQueuePage shipped at parity with the web
source: a pure @MainActor @Observable `FeedbackQueuePageModel` (ADR-004 — no
networking in the view) exposing the list state (loading/empty/error/success),
the status + category filter row, pagination, the row-expansion set, the per-row
GitHub-URL drafts, and the update lifecycle, over an injectable
`FeedbackQueueDataSource` seam whose value types mirror the web `FeedbackEntry` /
`FeedbackListResponse` / `FeedbackUpdateInput` 1:1 (production binds the KMP admin
endpoints). The page reproduces the web chrome (PageContainer title) and the single
GlassPanel (web GlassPanel1) that holds the filter row (Status + Category dropdowns,
Refresh with in-flight spinner, GitHub-bridge-disabled note) above the four-state
list — the loading spinner, the QueryError retry, the EmptyState, and the paginated,
expandable feedback table. Each expanded row reproduces the report body, the
submitter/agent metadata grid (with the reveal-on-demand masked email), the optional
recent_errors JSON + console-tail disclosures, and the inline triage action bar
(change status, paste/save a GitHub issue URL, forward to GitHub when the bridge is
configured). Every visible string resolves from Localizable.xcstrings via the web key
names (the translation.feedback.* / translation.common.* mirror — all 38 keys already
present in the catalog); date / em-dash / pretty-JSON / pageOf interpolation are
ported and unit-tested. The page is registered at the `.feedbackQueue` route (canonical
/feedback + the /admin/feedback alias) so the shell hosts + deep-links it in the System
group. The ported web hooks keep their names at the Swift call sites: `useFeedbackList`
-> `FeedbackQueueDataSource.loadFeedback`; `useUpdateFeedback` ->
`FeedbackQueueDataSource.updateFeedback`.

The AI triage advisor the web composes inside the expansion (AIFeedbackQueueTriage)
is a SEPARATE parity unit (component:AIFeedbackQueueTriage, already implemented under
TeslaSync/shared-surfaces) and is intentionally not re-embedded — it is not one of the
43 declared parity items for this page.

